<section class="wrap reveal" aria-labelledby="t-core-claims">
  <div class="page-head tight">
    <p class="kicker">Core claims</p>
    <h2 id="t-core-claims">Ten Claims, One Interdependent Framework</h2>
    <p class="lede muted">These are the load-bearing claims rather than every application of them. The
      purple diamond marks the framework&rsquo;s speculative reading: established mathematics may appear inside
      a claim without establishing the connection TTI draws from it.</p>
  </div>

  <ol class="core-claims">
    <li class="frame core-claim">
      <span class="claim-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
      <div class="claim-body">
        <h3><a href="/foundations/">Two asymmetric infinities frame reality</a> <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></h3>
        <p>TTI reads zero and one as boundary conditions between two asymptotic directions: the continuum
          toward zero and progression toward unbounded magnitude. Cantor&rsquo;s cardinal distinction is
          established mathematics; treating that asymmetry as a physical tilt, and the two limits as
          <a href="/temporal-antipodes/">opposite ends of time</a>, is the framework&rsquo;s conjecture.</p>
        <p class="claim-bridge"><strong>Interlink:</strong> the boundary conditions pose the relation that
          Claim 2 closes, while their asymmetry supplies the proposed direction used by Claim 6.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="frame core-claim">
      <span class="claim-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
      <div class="claim-body">
        <h3><a href="/foundations/#t-pi">π is the condition of closure</a> <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></h3>
        <p>A straight approach to an asymptote never returns. TTI therefore promotes π from the ratio found
          in circles to the condition by which an open relation bends back, becomes finite and can persist:
          existence is closure rather than an externally caused event.</p>
        <p class="claim-bridge"><strong>Interlink:</strong> closure converts Claim 1&rsquo;s open limits into a
          world; halving π opens Claim 3, and its second application becomes the return topology of
          Claim 8.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="frame core-claim">
      <span class="claim-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
      <div class="claim-body">
        <h3><a href="/foundations/#t-the-i-split">Halving π opens the complex plane</a> <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></h3>
        <p>Euler&rsquo;s established relation \(e^{i\pi/2}=i\) gives the quarter-turn into the imaginary axis.
          TTI reads that axis as dimensional opening; the resulting complex plane is the indispensable
          mathematical home of the quantum wavefunction.</p>
        <p class="claim-bridge"><strong>Interlink:</strong> Claim 2&rsquo;s closure produces the complex
          structure that Claim 4 treats as physical rather than merely descriptive.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="frame core-claim">
      <span class="claim-number" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
      <div class="claim-body">
        <h3><a href="/foundations/#t-chain">The wavefunction is matter, not only a description</a> <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></h3>
        <p>TTI chooses an ontic reading: complex amplitude is the physical substrate, and finite actuality
          is what remains when possibilities integrate, fail to cancel or become out of phase. This is an
          interpretation of quantum theory, not a derivation from it.</p>
        <p class="claim-bridge"><strong>Interlink:</strong> this is the junction. Integration branches toward
          the self in Claim 5, irreversible history in Claim 6, and physical accumulation in Claim 7.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="frame core-claim">
      <span class="claim-number" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
      <div class="claim-body">
        <h3><a href="/the-self/">Consciousness is the integral that makes a self</a> <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></h3>
        <p>Experience arrives as differential moments; consciousness is proposed as the operation that
          gathers them into a bounded, remembered first-person whole. Neural microtubules are offered as a
          possible biological site of that integration, not as an established solution to the hard problem.</p>
        <p class="claim-bridge"><strong>Interlink:</strong> Claim 5 applies Claim 4&rsquo;s integration at the
          experiential scale: matter and self are two outcomes of gathering, not two unrelated substances.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="frame core-claim">
      <span class="claim-number" aria-hidden="true">06</span>
      <div class="claim-body">
        <h3><a href="/seams/#t-arrow">Foundational asymmetry gives time a direction</a> <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></h3>
        <p>TTI identifies the arrow of time with the foundational tilt between the two infinities and with
          the information lost as open possibility becomes a closed history. It keeps thermodynamic and
          informational <a href="/entropy/">entropy distinct from its proposed integration phase</a>.</p>
        <p class="claim-bridge"><strong>Interlink:</strong> Claim 1 gives the tilt and Claim 4 gives the
          irreversible event; together they let Claims 7 and 8 speak about accumulation, memory and residue.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="frame core-claim">
      <span class="claim-number" aria-hidden="true">07</span>
      <div class="claim-body">
        <h3><a href="/gravity/">Mass and gravity are integration made geometric</a> <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></h3>
        <p>Gravity is read, consistently with general relativity, as curvature rather than a Newtonian force.
          TTI&rsquo;s extra claim is that mass records accumulated becoming. The bridge is incomplete: an
          <a href="/accumulated-differentials/">accumulation field</a> must acquire units, covariance,
          conserved stress&ndash;energy and a lawful coupling before it can weigh.</p>
        <p class="claim-bridge"><strong>Interlink:</strong> Claim 7 carries Claim 4&rsquo;s integration into
          spacetime physics and provides the curvature/completion scale later tabulated by Claim 9.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="frame core-claim">
      <span class="claim-number" aria-hidden="true">08</span>
      <div class="claim-body">
        <h3><a href="/torus/">Return is toroidal; inversion is Möbius</a> <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></h3>
        <p>The torus is the framework&rsquo;s shape of return with accumulation: a process can come home while
          retaining a winding count. The <a href="/moebius/">Möbius seam</a> is its orientation-reversing
          transition. A second ideal inversion restores orientation, so any surviving
          <a href="/double-inversion/">residue needs a declared carrier</a>. A
          <a href="/wormholes/">local wormhole interpretation</a> adds separate metric, energy, stability
          and causality requirements.</p>
        <p class="claim-bridge"><strong>Interlink:</strong> Claim 2 supplies closure and Claim 6 supplies
          directed history; Claim 8 gives both a topology of recurrence and the seam through which Claims 9
          and 10 propose observable residue.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="frame core-claim">
      <span class="claim-number" aria-hidden="true">09</span>
      <div class="claim-body">
        <h3><a href="/cosmic-ledger/">The cosmic budget records degrees of completion</a> <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></h3>
        <p>The Cosmic Ledger reads dark energy as baseline curvature, dark matter as integration sufficient
          to gravitate but not to carry luminous phase, and ordinary matter as completed complex phase. Its
          residues approximate 68.10 : 26.95 : 4.95, but the measurement function remains an ansatz.</p>
        <p class="claim-bridge"><strong>Interlink:</strong> the ledger combines Claim 3&rsquo;s phase, Claim 7&rsquo;s
          curvature and Claim 8&rsquo;s residue bookkeeping into one quantitative proposal.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="frame core-claim">
      <span class="claim-number" aria-hidden="true">10</span>
      <div class="claim-body">
        <h3><a href="/stress-tests/">The framework must expose seams where it can fail</a> <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></h3>
        <p>TTI proposes discriminating surfaces rather than treating resemblance as confirmation: an odd
          great-circle sign change in galaxy handedness, conservation and field-equation gates for
          accumulation, and the preregistered <a href="/little-red-dots/research-proposal/">Zero-Seam Test</a>
          against ordinary explanations of JWST little red dots.</p>
        <p class="claim-bridge"><strong>Interlink:</strong> Claim 10 is downstream of the other nine. If their
          links are physical, they must yield a result that competing accounts do not; if not, the chain is
          analogy rather than theory.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <div class="frame illuminated claim-map">
    <p class="kicker">How the links fit</p>
    <h3>The dependency map</h3>
    <p class="formula">\[
      (0,1)\xrightarrow{\text{closure}}\pi
      \xrightarrow{\text{halve }\pi}i
      \longrightarrow \mathbb{C}\longrightarrow\Psi
    \]</p>
    <ul class="claim-branches">
      <li><strong>Foundational spine:</strong> limits require closure; closure admits the complex structure;
        the framework then identifies the wavefunction with physical matter.</li>
      <li><strong>Integration branches:</strong> \(\Psi\) gathered as experience becomes the self;
        accumulation coupled through conserved \(T_{\mu\nu}\) could become mass and curvature.</li>
      <li><strong>Asymmetry branch:</strong> unequal limits plus irreversible integration give time a
        direction and allow history or residue to be discussed.</li>
      <li><strong>Topological branch:</strong> toroidal return retains winding, while Möbius transport tests
        what reverses, what returns and what could survive a cycle.</li>
      <li><strong>Cosmological synthesis:</strong> phase, curvature and residue become the Ledger&rsquo;s three
        completion states.</li>
      <li><strong>Empirical terminus:</strong> the claimed links earn physical force only where the
        stress tests and sky tests can distinguish them from existing accounts.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="muted small"><strong>Reading rule:</strong> an arrow records the framework&rsquo;s proposed order of
      dependence, not a proof that the item on the left uniquely entails the item on the right. The weakest
      links are the promoted physical meanings: closure as existence, wavefunction as matter, integration as
      self, accumulation as mass, and residues as the observed cosmic fractions.</p>
  </div>
</section>

